.TH 400SSD
.SH NAME
400ssd \- 400 SSD Term, a lightweight terminal emulator for X11
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B 400ssd
.RB [ \-v ]
.RB [ \-f
.IR font ]
.RB [ \-t
.IR title ]
.RB [ \-c
.IR class ]
.RB [ \-e
.IR command
.RI [ arguments ...]]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B 400ssd
is a small terminal emulator written in C on top of Xlib and Xft.
It is configured at compile time by editing
.IR config.h .
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-v
Print the version and exit.
.TP
.BI \-f " font"
Use the given fontconfig font description instead of the default.
.TP
.BI \-t " title"
Set the initial window title.
.TP
.BI \-c " class"
Set the WM_CLASS instance and class of the window.
.TP
.BI \-e " command " [ arguments ...]
Run the command instead of the shell. This option must be the last one.
.SH KEY BINDINGS
.TP
.B Ctrl+Shift+C
Copy the selection to the CLIPBOARD.
.TP
.B Ctrl+Shift+V
Paste from the CLIPBOARD.
.TP
.B Shift+Insert
Paste from the PRIMARY selection.
.TP
.B Shift+PageUp, Shift+PageDown
Scroll the history by one page.
.SH MOUSE
.TP
.B Left button
Select text. A double click selects a word and a triple click selects a line.
.TP
.B Middle button
Paste the PRIMARY selection.
.TP
.B Wheel
Scroll the history. On the alternate screen the wheel sends arrow keys.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B SHELL
Shell started when no command is given.
.PP
The child process receives TERM, COLORTERM and WINDOWID.
.SH CONFIGURATION
Edit
.I config.h
and rebuild. The file is created from
.I config.h.def
on the first build.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR xterm (1),
.BR fonts-conf (5)
